Keep it running.
CMD 2
mongo

Then:
use MYDB239720

The journal uses the database:
MYDB239720

and collection:
MyCol

Step 5 — Create insert.php
Inside:
C:\xampp\htdocs\Practical5\

create:
insert.php

Use the journal's code:
<?php

$m = new MongoClient();

echo "Connection to database successfully";

$db = $m->MYDB239720;

echo "\nDatabase selected successfully";

$col = $db->MyCol;

echo "\nCollection selected successfully";

$doc = array(
    "name" => "Romal",
    "age" => 20,
    "dept" => "TYIT",
    "rollno" => 239720
);

$col->insert($doc);

echo "\nDocument inserted successfully";

?>

The journal's insert.php uses the same database, collection and document fields.     BDNS Journal
